From 9266e722e0d96a7cf6d54317bf3043221f1f179d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 5 Aug 2026 19:25:13 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/4] Run the walkthrough on the real HCP protocol, at Lmax 4,
 6 and 8

Three changes asked for, plus one defect the real data exposed.

THE PROTOCOL IS NOW A REAL HCP SCHEME. protocol/hcp_real_3shell.txt is the
supplied FSL .bval/.bvec as tracked text, b divided by 1000 to reach the
ms/um^2 this package carries throughout. 288 volumes, 18 b~0 plus 90 each at
nominal b = 1, 2, 3; 90 distinct directions per shell, none shared between
shells. The synthetic hcp_like_3shell.txt stays for the published tables'
provenance but the walkthrough no longer uses it.

Real acquisitions differ from synthetic ones in ways the walkthrough now
shows rather than tidies away: the b = 0 volumes are b = 5 s/mm^2 and carry
unit direction vectors, and the b values jitter within each shell (18
distinct values). Step 1 now asks SMI's own
Group_dwi_in_shells_b_beta_TE to bin them and checks it recovers
[18 90 90 90], then uses that assignment for every per-shell number.

LMAX IS NOW EXPLICIT AND SWEPT. A dedicated section explains that the fit
runs at Lmax 4, 6 and 8 (15, 28 and 45 coefficients) while the ground truth
is fixed at 8 -- not a choice but SMI's kernel ceiling, since K_l is
undefined above l = 8. It states the consequence: at Lmax 8 the truth is
exactly representable by the fit, so that row is flattering and its
"ceiling" is no longer an independent bound. Step 7 scores each Lmax against
the truth truncated to that same Lmax.

STEP 8 IS NOW AN EXPORT, NOT A CROSS-CHECK. The sh2peaks comparison is gone.
Instead the fODF of each Lmax is written as an MRtrix SH image (CS_phase = 0,
so the coefficients need no conversion), with voxel_key.txt giving the true
fibre axes per voxel so a peak found in MRtrix can be matched back. The
walkthrough prints the commands and runs none of them.

THE DEFECT. The supplied .bvec is unit only to 1.1e-6, being written at
7 significant figures. SMI.get_even_SH normalises internally; treating g(3)
as cos(theta) does not, so the Step 3 zonal-vs-forward-model identity broke
at 5.8e-7 instead of 1e-15. Isolated to the direction set by holding b fixed
and swapping direction sets, then confirmed: normalising on load restores
8.9e-16. This could only have been found on real data.

Also fixed: per-shell masks used |b - b_nominal| < 0.5*b_nominal, which for
b = 2 admits b = 2.98 and silently mixed the b = 3 shell into it -- visible
as a nearest-neighbour spacing of 7.0 deg where it should be 12.7.

