From 451990b57d084ef7581eb6f21da156e501ba30cf Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 5 Aug 2026 19:34:50 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/4] Move the whole package onto the real HCP protocol, and
 warn loudly

Two changes asked for.

ONE PROTOCOL, READ THROUGH ONE FUNCTION. mc_config.m gains PROTOCOL and
load_protocol(), and gen_montecarlo.m, sweep_nonneg.m and the walkthrough
all read the acquisition through it instead of loading bvals/bvecs from
binio's gitignored data/. The package now runs on the real HCP scheme
everywhere, not just in the walkthrough.

protocol/hcp_like_3shell.txt, the synthetic scheme, is kept but its header
now opens with SUPERSEDED and states that nothing reads it and that every
number in Reports/ was measured on it. Deleting it would strand the
provenance of the published tables; regenerating those tables is now a
re-run rather than a code change.

THE .bvec WARNING IS LOUD, NOT SILENT. Previously the walkthrough normalised
the directions and mentioned it in passing. The warning now lives in
load_protocol(), so it fires for the pipeline too and cannot be bypassed by
reading the file directly: a banner with the measured max||g|-1| = 1.13e-06,
what is being done about it, and what it costs if it is not -- the Lmax 8
zonal-response identity degrading from ~1e-15 to ~5e-7.

Documentation follows: both READMEs describe the real protocol and the three
real-acquisition properties the walkthrough checks rather than assumes (b=0
volumes are b=5 s/mm^2 with meaningless unit directions, b jitters within
shells so SMI's own binning is checked to recover [18 90 90 90], and the
.bvec is unit only to 1e-6). Stale claims corrected: the walkthrough takes
about six minutes now that it fits three angular orders, not two, and
setup_protocol.py is described as producing the evaluation sphere since it
no longer supplies the protocol in use.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01GptEuETZEw1QVJAj7e9vag
