From 5fd3ada2494673ed808ec05c2871edf335ffe639 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 5 Aug 2026 19:40:10 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 4/4] Add figures for geometry, kernel, signal and
 reconstructed fODFs

A Figures section between Step 8 and Step 9, drawing the four things the
walkthrough produces, in the order they happen:

  1. ground truth fibre geometry -- one glyph per condition
  2. the kernel as a response function -- angular profile per shell, the
     zonal coefficients as a bar chart (an MRtrix response file), and the
     response glyph at the highest shell
  3. forward convolution and noise -- signal against angle to the first
     fibre, noisy over noise-free, one panel per shell
  4. the reconstructed fODFs -- a grid of Lmax against condition

Glyphs go through SMI_response_helpers, so radius is |amplitude| and colour
is the SIGNED amplitude. That is deliberate: the band-limited truth really
is negative over much of the sphere, and a renderer that folded the sign
away would hide the one result in this file most likely to surprise.

MAKE_FIGURES = false skips the section.

Rendering is NOT verified here: Octave's print is broken in this container,
so what was checked is that the block executes end to end against the
repository's graphics stubs -- i.e. the indexing, the glyph calls and the
reconstruction of plm from the fitted SH coefficients are right, and only
the drawing itself is untested. In MATLAB the figures appear inline in the
Live Script.

